# PLACEHOLDER PATCH — ffmpeg-ohos.patch
#
# This file intentionally contains NO diff hunks, so build-deps.sh detects it
# as a placeholder and skips it (see apply_patches()). Do not delete it: it
# documents where and how to put the real fix when FFmpeg fails to build
# against musl/OHOS.
#
# How to use:
#   1. Run build-deps.sh --only ffmpeg and inspect
#      <work-dir>/logs/ffmpeg.log for the first real error.
#   2. Edit the extracted sources under <work-dir>/ffmpeg-7.1/ to fix it.
#   3. From that directory: git diff > <repo>/build-aux/harmony/patches/ffmpeg-ohos.patch
#      (or `diff -ruN pristine fixed > ffmpeg-ohos.patch`). Paths must apply
#      with `patch -p1` (a/ b/ prefixes are fine).
#   4. Re-run build-deps.sh --only ffmpeg --fresh.
#
# What typically needs patching when porting FFmpeg 7.x to a musl/OHOS target
# configured as --target-os=linux (all are guesses until the first real build;
# keep this list as a debugging map):
#
#   * HAVE_* misdetections: configure compiles probes with the cross CC, but
#     a few checks test glibc-only facilities that musl declares in headers
#     yet does not implement (or implements differently), e.g. sys/sysctl.h
#     based code paths, malloc_trim(), GNU-specific pthread options. Symptom:
#     undefined symbol at link time — the OHOS toolchain links with
#     -Wl,--no-undefined, so this is a hard error, not a warning. Fix by
#     forcing the HAVE_ macro off via a patch to config.h generation or by
#     #if defined(__GLIBC__) guards around the call site.
#
#   * libavutil/mem.c and friends: alignment/allocation helpers that assume
#     glibc behavior (aligned_alloc availability/semantics, posix_memalign
#     errno details). musl provides the POSIX APIs but edge cases differ.
#
#   * Missing/renamed syscall plumbing: sys/syscall.h constants (SYS_*) used
#     under #ifdef __linux__ that OHOS's musl fork does not define (e.g.
#     prctl-adjacent code, pidfd, getrandom fallbacks). Guard with
#     #ifdef SYS_xxx or __OHOS__ checks.
#
#   * clock/thread CPU-affinity APIs (sched_setaffinity, pthread_getname_np
#     signature differences) used by libavcodec/pthread_*.c and the aarch64
#     cpu detection code.
#
#   * If arm64 assembly (.S under libavcodec/aarch64/) fails to assemble
#     with the OHOS clang 15, first try building with --disable-asm added in
#     deps/ffmpeg.sh to confirm asm is the culprit before patching.
